# Trivy allowlist for known/accepted CVEs (PETPLAT-105).
#
# Used by .github/workflows/build-push.yml's Trivy scan steps via the
# trivyignores input (this file). Entries here are suppressed from BOTH the
# CRITICAL,HIGH report and the CRITICAL-only gate — so a CRITICAL CVE listed
# here will NOT fail the build.
#
# How to add an entry:
#   1. Confirm the CVE is a false positive, unexploitable in how this image
#      is actually used, or has no upstream fix yet and the risk is accepted.
#   2. Add one line per CVE ID below, with a comment explaining why.
#   3. Re-run the pipeline to confirm the build now passes.
#   4. Revisit periodically — remove the entry once a real fix is available
#      upstream (check: `trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH {image}` locally).
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, e.g.:
# CVE-2023-12345  # reason this is accepted, and since when

# --- TEMPORARY: GitOps loop test (PETPLAT-116, 2026-10-03) ---
